ently checked. The integrated Jensen comparison bounds the true near-one density increment from the uniform vertical mollified second moment, with an explicit squared center error and no unit-spacing hypothesis. A second comparison supplies an unconditional finite-energy bound with the Euler and pole terms retained. The dyadic refinement charges each frequency block its own length in the off-diagonal term. The Gaussian bound charges each coefficient its own index and the interval half-width, with no dyadic summation or block-count factor. The general compact contour shift gives the exact mollified error with both residues. The smoothed tail stops at the smoothing cutoff, and the weighted critical-product second moment retains the three logarithms in the off-diagonal mollifier fourth moment. An unconditional comparison extends the fifth-log Ingham density bound to the explicit shrinking strip with (1-sigma) log T >= 55 log(1+log T), and covers the explicit zero-free range. The historical prime-gap exponent proofs remain open."
